  "category": "Uncategorized",
  "description": "add github action to build and run tests\n\nTechnical Implementation:\n\n**GitHub Actions Workflow Structure:**\n- File location: `.github/workflows/ci.yml`\n- Trigger events: `push` (main, develop branches), `pull_request` (to main, develop)\n- Matrix strategy: Test across Python 3.9, 3.10, 3.11, and 3.12\n- Separate jobs: lint, test (CPU-only), test-gpu (optional)\n\n**Build Process Steps:**\n1. Checkout code with submodules for any ML model weights\n2. Set up Python environment using `actions/setup-python`\n3. Cache pip dependencies with hash from `requirements.txt` and `setup.py`\n4. Install system dependencies: `ffmpeg`, `libgl1`, `libglib2.0-0` (required for OpenCV)\n5. Install Python dependencies: `pip install -r requirements.txt[dev]`\n6. Verify installation: `python -c \"import torch; import cv2; print('OK')\"`\n\n**Linting and Code Quality:**\n- Run `black --check .` for code formatting\n- Run `ruff check .` for linting\n- Optionally: `mypy .` for type checking\n- Fail fast on linting errors before running tests\n\n**Testing Configuration:**\n- Use `pytest` as test runner with `pytest-cov` for coverage\n- Parallel execution: `pytest -n auto` (via pytest-xdist)\n- Coverage reporting: `--cov=. --cov-report=xml --cov-report=term`\n- Test discovery pattern: `tests/**/*.py`\n- JUnit XML output for GitHub Actions parsing: `--junitxml=test-results.xml`\n\n**GPU Testing (Conditional):**\n- Separate job with `runs-on: self-hosted` or `ubuntu-latest` with CUDA runner\n- Trigger condition: `contains(github.event.head_commit.message, '[gpu-test]')` or manual workflow dispatch\n- Install CUDA toolkit and cuDNN\n- Set `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0` environment variable\n- Run GPU-specific tests with marker: `pytest -m \"requires_gpu\"`\n\n**Dependency Caching Strategy:**\n```yaml\n- name: Cache pip packages\n  uses: actions/cache@v3\n  with:\n    path: ~/.cache/pip\n    key: ${{ runner.os }}-pip-${{ hashFiles('**/requirements.txt') }}\n    restore-keys: |\n      ${{ runner.os }}-pip-\n```\n\n**Artifact Handling:**\n- Upload test results: `actions/upload-artifact` for `test-results.xml`\n- Upload coverage reports: `codecov` action or Codecov upload\n- Build artifacts: None (test-only pipeline)\n\n**Security and Secrets:**\n- Store cloud storage credentials (AWS S3, GCS) as GitHub Secrets\n- Use encrypted secrets for API keys (if cloud integration tests exist)\n- Mask sensitive outputs in logs\n\n**Performance Optimizations:**\n- Set `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` to avoid .pyc files\n- Use `pip install --no-cache-dir` for cleaner builds\n- Limit parallel test execution to avoid OOM: `pytest -n 4`\n\n**Notification:**\n- Use `actions/github-script` to comment on PRs with test results\n- Fail the workflow if coverage drops below threshold (e.g., 80%)\n- Set status checks required for merge protection\n\n**Docker Integration (Optional):**\n- Job to build Docker image from `Dockerfile`\n- Run tests inside container to match production environment\n- Push image to registry on tag/release\n\n**Workflow Example Structure:**\n```yaml\nname: CI\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [ main, develop ]\n  pull_request:\n    branches: [ main, develop ]\n\njobs:\n  lint:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps: [checkout, setup-python, cache, install-deps, run-black, run-ruff]\n  \n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        python-version: ['3.9', '3.10', '3.11', '3.12']\n    steps: [checkout, setup-python, cache, install-deps, install-system-libs, run-tests]\n```\n\n**Integration Points:**\n- Existing pytest configuration in `pytest.ini` or `pyproject.toml`\n- Requirements files: `requirements.txt`, `requirements-dev.txt`\n- Coverage configuration in `.coveragerc` or `pyproject.toml`",
